## :image: What it looked like

![A South Bronx street in the 1970s](https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5c/RIFF_170_during_the_1970%27s.jpg)

> Half a million people left the borough between 1970 and 1980. What stayed: the churches, the bodegas, the block associations that would rebuild it.

---

## :sprout: The comeback

- 1980s and 90s: [Charlotte Gardens](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlotte_Street_(Bronx)), ranch houses on the rubble; the Ten-Year Plan rebuilt a hundred thousand homes
- Community land trusts, the Banana Kelly block, the Bronx River cleaned
- 2009: a new Yankee Stadium; the old one's footprint a park

> The Bronx is the fastest-growing borough again; the question of the 2020s is who the growth is for.

---

